        "transcriptHtml": "<p class=\"transcript-note\">Automatic transcript. It may contain small recognition errors; the answer key is authoritative.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[00:00]</span> You will hear two students, Jacinta and Lewis, discussing a holiday they are planning in Queenstown, a tourist center in New Zealand, popular with young people. First you have some time to look at questions one to six, now we shall begin. You should answer the questions as you listen, because you will not hear the recording a</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[00:50]</span> second time. Open carefully and answer questions one to six. Hi Lewis, it&#x27;s Jacinta here. Oh hi Jacinta, I was just going to call you.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[01:11]</span> I was thinking we ought to do something about accommodation for our trip to Queenstown. Yeah, actually that&#x27;s just why I rang you. I&#x27;ve been looking on the internet, there was one place that looked ok called Travelers Lodge, but when I checked availability for January, when we&#x27;re planning to go, I found</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[01:29]</span> it was fully booked. Right, well we&#x27;d better do something now I suppose. I&#x27;ve actually got a list up here on the computer. There&#x27;s one place called Bingles, that looks possible, it&#x27;s $19.75 a night, that&#x27;s US dollars,</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[01:47]</span> they quote all the prices in US dollars. So that&#x27;s about twenty six or twenty seven New Zealand dollars, that&#x27;s ok, that&#x27;ll be in a dormitory is it? Yeah, they say eight-bed dorms and the hostel&#x27;s right in the town centre and they&#x27;ve got</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[02:03]</span> a cafe, they have theme nights every weekend, whatever that means. Oh you know, like certain sorts of food and music, and people might wear special clothes like that Egyptian evening we went to last year. Oh, ok, what else?</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[02:19]</span> They&#x27;ve got a sun deck area and then all the usual things, internet access and so on. Sounds good. Is there anywhere else? Yeah, a couple more places.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[02:31]</span> There&#x27;s one called Shale Lodge, which is just eighteen US dollars, that&#x27;s for a bed in a twelve-bed dorm, they do single and family rooms as well. It looks as if it&#x27;s a bit out of town, says it&#x27;s got an alpine setting, a quiet alpine setting, what do you think?</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[02:52]</span> Not sure. Oh, but actually it&#x27;s not far out at all, it says ten minutes walk from town so, ah, and it says it&#x27;s children friendly. Ah, I&#x27;m not so sure about that, what about the third place?</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[03:10]</span> That&#x27;s called Globetrotters, let&#x27;s see, they do private rooms or five-bed dorms for eighteen fifty. It&#x27;s in the centre, just by the lake, and that includes breakfast. Didn&#x27;t the other two?</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[03:26]</span> I don&#x27;t think so, they didn&#x27;t mention it, so probably not. Oh, and it says something about a free skydive, wow. Don&#x27;t know if I&#x27;m all that keen on jumping out of air planes. Ah, actually what it says is you can win a chance to do a skydive.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[03:45]</span> They give one away every day to one of the guests. Well, if I win it, you can do it. Anyway, do they have room? Yeah, I&#x27;d check the availability, shall I go ahead and book that in?</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[03:57]</span> Fine. You now have some time to look at questions seven-t. Now listen, and answer questions seven to ten. I was looking at what there is to do too, there are lots of sites offering deals for</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[04:40]</span> adventure sports, I suppose we have to do a bungee jump. Why? Well, it&#x27;s Cranestown where they more or less started it as a sport. You can, if you really want to jump off the side of a bridge with an elastic rope tied</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[04:54]</span> round your ankles. I&#x27;ll watch. OK, so what do you want to do? As far as adventure sports go, I was talking to someone who went whitewater rafting there.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[05:07]</span> He said it was really awesome. They drive you up the shot over river, and then you come down on a rubber raft through the whitewater rapids, where the river&#x27;s really narrow and fast, and end up going through a tunnel nearly two hundred metres long.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[05:21]</span> I think it&#x27;s quite expensive though. Oh, I&#x27;m on for that if you are. Cool. The other thing you can do is the jet boat ride.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[05:31]</span> That sounded just a lot of noise though. It&#x27;s basically just whizzing round on the river on a very fast boat, isn&#x27;t it? My friend did that as well. He said it was a bit touristy, but worth it.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[05:43]</span> I&#x27;ll give it a go. You go right up the river canyon. He said the drivers were really skillful, but I don&#x27;t mind going on my own. But there&#x27;s lots to do as well as a whole commercial adventure, but we ought to do some</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[05:56]</span> trekking. The scenery round there is amazing. I don&#x27;t want to miss that. The place to start is Glunalki, apparently, about 40 minutes drive.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[06:05]</span> That&#x27;s where a lot of the wilderness trails begin. OK. I&#x27;ll pack my walking boots, I better start getting in training. I haven&#x27;t done anything except sit at my desk for months.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[06:16]</span> Now is there anything else we need to decide? That is the end of section one. You now have half a minute to check your answers. Now turn to section two.</p>"
